# Arduino Wiki

> Official Arduino documentation and resources. Arduino is an open-source electronics platform based on easy-to-use hardware and software, used worldwide for learning, prototyping, and building interactive projects.

Arduino designs, manufactures, and supports electronic devices and software, allowing people around the world to easily access advanced technologies that interact with the physical world. The platform serves students, makers, educators, and professional developers across Maker, Education, and Pro segments.

